Kernel-build-only stand-ins for the hosted headers that
native/capability/aienos_capability.c, aienos_contain.c and
native/argus/bridge/argus_aegis_bridge.c include (pthread.h, stdio.h,
stdlib.h, time.h, string.h). They are put on the include path ONLY for the
freestanding kernel build (first entry of STAGE_CFLAGS in stage.mk); host tests use the real
libc and pthreads. Every name is redirected to a ck_compat_* function in
../ck_compat.c, built on ck.h services:
  malloc/calloc/free  -> ck_alloc / ck_free
  clock_gettime       -> ck_time_us
  fopen("/dev/urandom") + fread -> the CPU RNDR instruction when present,
                         else a timer-jitter fallback that is announced on the
                         console as WEAK (the capability office token)
  pthread_mutex_*     -> single-core flag; contention means a bug (re-entry)
                         and panics instead of deadlocking.
The native/* sources are compiled unmodified.
